---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Stainless Steel Wire Mesh (304/316) — Specs, Prices & Anping Factories" description="Stainless steel woven wire mesh: 304 vs 316, mesh sizes 1–635, wire diameter, weight and open area. Source direct from Anping factories.">
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 prose">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-steel-900">Stainless Steel Wire Mesh</h1>
    <p>Stainless steel woven mesh is the workhorse of industrial filtration and screening. Anping factories weave it from 1 mesh (heavy quarry screen) down to 635 mesh (pharmaceutical-grade), in rolls typically 1 m wide × 30 m long.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-steel-900">304 vs 316</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Grade</th><th>Ni / Cr</th><th>Corrosion resistance</th><th>Typical use</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>304</td><td>8% Ni, 18% Cr</td><td>Good — indoor & general outdoor</td><td>Filtration, screening, food contact</td></tr>
        <tr><td>316 / 316L</td><td>10–14% Ni, 16–18% Cr + Mo</td><td>Excellent — marine & chemical</td><td>Coastal, chemical processing, pharma</td></tr>
        <tr><td>304 is ~15–20% cheaper than 316</td><td colspan="3" class="text-steel-500">Unless you need Mo-grade corrosion resistance, 304 is the default.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-steel-900">Common specifications</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Mesh</th><th>Wire (mm)</th><th>Opening (mm)</th><th>Weight (kg/m²)</th><th>Application</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>8</td><td>0.7</td><td>2.48</td><td>2.76</td><td>Filter support</td></tr>
        <tr><td>20</td><td>0.4</td><td>0.87</td><td>1.58</td><td>Water filtration</td></tr>
        <tr><td>40</td><td>0.25</td><td>0.39</td><td>0.97</td><td>Oil / liquid filtration</td></tr>
        <tr><td>60</td><td>0.19</td><td>0.23</td><td>0.70</td><td>Fine filtration</td></tr>
        <tr><td>100</td><td>0.10</td><td>0.154</td><td>0.49</td><td>Standard filter cloth</td></tr>
        <tr><td>200</td><td>0.05</td><td>0.077</td><td>0.25</td><td>Pharmaceutical</td></tr>
        <tr><td>325</td><td>0.035</td><td>0.043</td><td>0.22</td><td>Lab sieving</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="text-sm text-steel-500">Weights are theoretical plain-weave values. <a href="/tools/woven-wire-mesh-weight-calculator/" class="text-accent-600">Calculate any spec →</a></p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-steel-900">What to specify when ordering</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Grade: 304 or 316 (ask for a material test certificate — MTC)</li>
      <li>Mesh count and wire diameter in mm (avoid gauge-only specs)</li>
      <li>Weave: plain, twill (for &gt;100 mesh heavy wire), or Dutch weave</li>
      <li>Roll width and length; edges selvage or cut</li>
      <li>Quantity in m² or kg — factories quote per kg for woven mesh</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-steel-900">FAQ</h2>
    <details class="mb-3"><summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">How is woven mesh priced?</summary><p class="text-sm mt-2">By weight (USD/kg) plus weaving complexity. Finer mesh with thin wire costs more per kg because weaving is slower. Dutch weave is the most expensive.</p></details>
    <details class="mb-3"><summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">Typical MOQ?</summary><p class="text-sm mt-2">Stock specs: 1 roll. Custom spec: usually 100–500 m². Anping factories are flexible on first orders to win long-term buyers.</p></details>
    <details class="mb-3"><summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">How do I verify it's real stainless steel?</summary><p class="text-sm mt-2">Request MTC from the wire rod batch, and do a spot PMI test or magnet check on samples (304 is weakly magnetic after cold drawing — a strong magnet sticking hard suggests low-grade steel).</p></details>

    <div class="not-prose mt-8 bg-steel-900 text-white rounded-xl p-6">
      <p class="font-semibold text-lg">Get quotes from Anping stainless mesh factories</p>
      <a href="/inquiry/" class="inline-block mt-3 bg-accent-500 hover:bg-accent-600 font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg transition-colors">Send an inquiry →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
